2026-10-09T02:14:59.7853817Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7954129Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7964290Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7965402Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7966257Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7966910Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7967219Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7967743Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7968240Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7968671Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7969344Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7969995Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7970813Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7971359Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7971804Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7972139Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7972300Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7972516Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7972765Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7973037Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7973403Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7973527Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7973636Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7973789Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7974150Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7974957Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7978919Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7979087Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7979315Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7979673Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7980422Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7981250Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7981942Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7982382Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7982843Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7983783Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7984406Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7994814Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:59.7995700Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8007711Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8008631Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8009225Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8010005Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8010713Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8027493Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8028507Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8039121Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8039925Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8040391Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8040582Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8040924Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8041298Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8041750Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8042508Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8042864Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8043052Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8043527Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8043808Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8044159Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T02:14:59.8044908Z   $ sh ./install-nix
